{
  "rule": "Lines that are neither blank nor comments of the code that builds and launches each pipeline. NPPDx: the __global__ kernel and the device helpers it calls, the structs that define the types of its operations and tiles (whole), its launch configuration (init with cudaFuncSetAttribute, grid, block, shared memory, the launch and its error check) and its list of tile and block configurations. FKL: the call that builds and launches the pipeline (executeOperations, executeBoxBlur, executeLinearFilter) with the operation chains it is given, the details and tile list of a DPP, the intermediates of a staged form with their views and coefficient images, and the error check of the call. Not counted on either side: the harness (Implementation/stage wrappers, beforeKernel hooks, timing, CSV, modes), the host references, validation, the sweeps that choose a configuration, the output buffers, the parameter structures, constants and aliases shared by every version or derived from the workload (Normalization, crop origins, RESIZE_J/K, HALO, YUVToRGB, the Spec alias and the K, PASSES, halo and GAUSSIAN members of the Spec structs, the taps() accessor used by FKL and the references), the namespace and include lines, and, counting per program, the branches that the program of a row does not instantiate together with their if/else dispatch lines (the 8-bit write branch of Experiment 3's kernel; the two-pass branch of the part (c) kernel for the one-pass programs and the one-pass branch for the two-pass program; the box/Gaussian and one/two-pass dispatch of the shared FKL functions). BoxBVF and GaussianBVF, operations written for the benchmark, are counted apart. Calibration: FKL 10, NPPDx 109, NPPDx+NPP 131 at 3845b60 (results-v3-addendum/README.md section 4).",
